'''Avatar Testing Chamber''' is a cross-platform [[Special:MyLanguage/:Category:Worlds|world]] created by {{VRC link|https://vrchat.com/home/user/usr_d37acd76-341a-46af-9b0e-d5b0ffa2181d|Ziggor}}. Players can test avatar lighting, mesh visualization, animation, mirrors, and related tools. Menus are in English or Japanese.

== Layout ==

The world is an indoor testing chamber. Players spawn among mirrors, chairs, a video screen, and wall menus for world settings, language, and testing tools. A photo backdrop and colour box stand in a photo area. Realtime lights, projectors, and a doppelganger occupy the floor. This world is an open testing area.

A keypad opens a hidden area in a wall. The passcode is 852, matching a radio labelled 85.2 FM.

== Features ==

Menus toggle colliders, a join bell, a fade menu, brightness, night mode, chairs, and a radio. A custom pedestal equips an avatar from an avatar ID. Weighted cubes, photo objects, and pens sit on tables and can be reset.

Progress for settings, statistics, and achievements saves with [[Special:MyLanguage/Persistence|Persistence]]. Join-streak counters reset at midnight.

=== Lighting ===

Realtime lights include directional, point, spot, and a rotating point light {{formatnum:1.5}} m off the floor. Sliders set colour hue, temperature, intensity, range, shadow type, and related values. Settings can be copied as a shareable code. Sky can be day or night.

[[Special:MyLanguage/Community:VRC Light Volumes|Light Volumes]] and LTCGI light the space. Projectors include an emissions and LTCGI plane.

=== Mesh and avatar tools ===

Projectors overlay wireframe (triangles or quads), normals, tangent space, vertex density, X-ray, backface, checkers, bones, matcap, UV, and depth. A contacts stick and a raycast wall test avatar contacts and collisions. The raycast wall is off until enabled from the menu.

A scale control and auto-height display measure the current avatar. Post-processing and ambient occlusion toggles include a depth option for avatars that lack DepthGet.

=== Animation ===

Stations play walk cycles (basic, alluring, cool, static, tiptoe), crawls, a "crazy walk," and two run loops. A platform triggers a falling animation if the avatar has one. An [[wikipedia:MikuMikuDance|MMD]] dance area plays a recorded motion; jumping exits it.

=== Mirrors and doppelganger ===

[[Special:MyLanguage/Mirrors|Mirrors]] include a fade mirror, a static toggle, a 2D mirror, and a PC mirror. A doppelganger shows a duplicate of the current avatar that can be scaled. A 2D audio zone lets players talk in 2D.

=== Photo area ===

The photo screen and a colour box take a colour from a wall pen or a hex field. Camera views include front, back, left, right, and rotations. Photo objects and a seated photo chair are in the area.

=== Audio and video ===

A video player supports URL playback and texture streaming. [[Special:MyLanguage/Community:AudioLink|AudioLink]] is present on PC and Android.

=== Achievements and statistics ===

Player statistics and achievements track joins, time in the world, join streaks, distance walked, jumps, respawns, and avatar swaps. Achievements also include sharing an instance with a set number of people, finding the open testing area, finding a hidden area in a wall, holding a weighted cube, or breaking a security camera.

=== World store ===

The world is enrolled in the [[Special:MyLanguage/Creator Economy|Creator Economy]]. The world store sells a Tip Jar listing for 100 credits. A Default Cube group listing for 100 credits unlocks a Companion Cube; if one player in the instance unlocks it, the rest of the instance can see it. Other Default Cube group listings put the buyer's name on supporter lists in Ziggor's worlds.

